;; bedit-theme-dracula — a Dracula colour theme for the bedit editor, as a hive
;; PLUGIN package. It declares `:enhances {bedit ">= 0.3"}` (Debian's `Enhances:`
;; — "I add functionality to bedit", checked by the host, never a hard dependency)
;; and ships pure data: an entry module exposing `(bedit-plugin)`, the contribution
;; map bedit folds into its theme picker. No `:dependencies` — a theme plugin never
;; touches the editor's code, only contributes a palette, so it stays a leaf.
;;
;; Publish:  nest publish
;; Use:      in a bedit checkout, `nest add bedit-theme-dracula :version "^0.2"`
;;           then reopen the editor — "Dracula" appears in `M-x theme-select`.
(project
  :name "bedit-theme-dracula"
  :version "0.2.0"
  :brood ">= 0.13.0"
  :description
    "A Dracula colour theme for the bedit editor — a plugin package (:enhances bedit). Pure data: a 16-role palette the host folds into M-x theme-select."
  :repository "https://github.com/broodlang/bedit-theme-dracula"
  :enhances {bedit ">= 0.3"}
  :source-paths ["src"])
